      {
        "heading": "Accidents and incidents",
        "text": "On May 18, 1926, in Argo, Illinois , a Ford Air Transport 2-AT Maiden Deaborn I was involved in the first fatal accident for a commercial U.S. aircraft. The Contract Air Mail pilot crashed and was killed due to flight into poor weather conditions. On May 12, 1928, a Ford Air Freight 4-AT-01 , NC 1492 crashed on takeoff from Dearborn Michigan killing the only two passengers on board the aircraft."
      }
